  "resolution_rules": [
    "Operation #/model_definitions_selector is a symbolic catalog selector; MODEL_TYPE_SOURCE_SPECIFICATION.json resolves to this named_catalogs exact pin, not the operations/ directory.",
    "Unit relative source references resolve from their source file directory; adopted source filenames resolve within their pinned adopted subject root.",
    "Absolute local Archive locators remain original evidence locators and are not public URLs or an authorization to read arbitrary paths.",
    "A publication path-map must preserve raw hash and declared pointer/dialect/version; a derived index never replaces the canonical contract bytes.",
    "Unsupported selector, source hash mismatch or absent required body yields HOLD; never guess a latest file.",
    "For public-only reading, normalize only slash direction in an original locator then consult the pinned PUBLICATION_LOCATOR_COMPANION exact map. Require declared raw hash, source commit and encoding; never use basename or newest-version fallback.",
    "Original C:/D: Markdown href bytes are historical locators. Use source_file plus markdown_link_ordinal in accepted_entry_markdown_links to open the exact pinned public target; this does not rewrite or replace the accepted file.",
    "A path-map entry is not proof of required execution input availability. PRIVATE_RETAINED, unresolved historical references or applicable current required bodies missing mean HOLD for that specific use; retain REFERENCE_DOMAIN_DISPOSITION distinctions.",
    "JSON pointers decode only RFC6901 ~1 and ~0 with exact list indices. Symbolic MODEL_TYPE_SOURCE_SPECIFICATION.json#/definition_lookup/<name> uses the named catalog and replaces <name> only by an exact declared model name; unknown is rejected.",
    "gzip is storage transport only: verify storage hash then decompress and verify canonical raw hash before JSON/pointer use. A raw whole-file hash never equals a declared canonical JSON hash or historical line-slice hash unless explicitly verified in its own domain.",
    "No qualified runtime resolver is implemented or activated by this navigation supplement; no C3, RQ03, host injection, execution, admission or acceptance qualification is inferred."
